// Chapter 1, Tony the bulldog runs the bodega downstairs.
// Every option runs <<choose "id">>; its effects live in Content/storylets_ch1.json.
// Russian text lives in Chapter1-ru.csv; keep #line ids stable.

title: ch1_tony_intro
---
A bulldog in a stained apron is wrestling a pallet of soda through the bodega door downstairs. #line:ch1_tony_intro_01
Tony: You. New kid from upstairs. You got arms? #line:ch1_tony_intro_02
-> Grab the other end. #line:ch1_tony_intro_03
    <<choose "help">>
    Tony: Strong and polite. Rare combo. Name's Tony. Coffee's on me this week. #line:ch1_tony_intro_04
-> Sorry, I'm late for a shift. #line:ch1_tony_intro_05
    <<choose "busy">>
    Tony: Everybody's late for something. #line:ch1_tony_intro_06
===

title: ch1_tony_snacks
---
Tony: I got forty boxes of granola bars that expire next week. The distributor won't take them back. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_01
Tony: Ten bucks a box. You resell them, we both win. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_02
-> Sell them cheap and say they expire soon. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_03
    <<choose "honest">>
    Customers love a deal they understand. The boxes are gone in two days. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_04
-> Peel off the dates and sell them as fresh. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_05
    <<choose "relabel">>
    You make double. You also check the reviews more often than you'd like to admit. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_06
-> Pass. Not my business. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_07
    <<choose "pass">>
    Tony: Suit yourself. #line:ch1_tony_snacks_08
===

title: ch1_tony_robbery
---
Morning. The bodega window is a spiderweb of cracks. Someone broke in overnight and took the register. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_01
Tony: Insurance covers the glass. Not the week I'm closed. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_02
-> Chip in a hundred fifty for repairs. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_03
    <<choose "chip_in">>
    Tony: I don't forget things like this. Ever. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_04
-> Spend Saturday helping him clean up. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_05
    <<choose "clean">>
    Tony: Sweeping glass with a friend beats sweeping it alone. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_06
-> Not my problem. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_07
    <<choose "ignore">>
    Tony walks past you on the stairs without a word. #line:ch1_tony_robbery_08
===

title: ch1_tony_shelf
---
Tony: I been thinking. That shelf by the register? Yours. Put your resale stuff there. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_01
Tony: I take ten percent. Family discount. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_02
-> Deal. Shake on it. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_03
    <<choose "accept">>
    Your first retail spot. It's two feet wide and it smells like coffee. It's perfect. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_04
-> Thanks, but I'm not ready. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_05
    <<choose "decline">>
    Tony: Offer stands. #line:ch1_tony_shelf_06
===

title: ch1_tony_fallout
---
A one-star review. The granola tasted like cardboard and somebody's kid got a stomach ache. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_01
The post has three hundred shares and your shop name in the first line. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_02
-> Refund everyone and apologize publicly. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_03
    <<choose "refund">>
    It costs you. Two customers reply that they respect the honesty. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_04
-> Deny everything. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_05
    <<choose "deny">>
    The comments get worse. Screenshots don't lie. #line:ch1_tony_fallout_06
===

title: ch1_tony_cold
---
Tony: No tab for you. Cash only. #line:ch1_tony_cold_01
You remember every time you said you were busy. #line:ch1_tony_cold_02
-> Apologize and offer to help this weekend. #line:ch1_tony_cold_03
    <<choose "apologize">>
    Tony: Saturday, seven sharp. Bring gloves. #line:ch1_tony_cold_04
-> Shrug and pay cash. #line:ch1_tony_cold_05
    <<choose "shrug">>
    Tony: Next. #line:ch1_tony_cold_06
===

title: ch1_tony_dinner
---
Tony: Sunday. Family dinner at my place. You're coming, no excuses. #line:ch1_tony_dinner_01
-> Go. Bring dessert. #line:ch1_tony_dinner_02
    <<choose "go">>
    Six cousins, one table, zero talk about work. You laugh until your face hurts. #line:ch1_tony_dinner_03
-> Pick up a dinner shift instead. #line:ch1_tony_dinner_04
    <<choose "work">>
    The tips are good. The empty seat at Tony's table is noticed. #line:ch1_tony_dinner_05
===
